openssl-rs — provenance notice
==============================

This project reconstructs the externally observable contract of OpenSSL in
native Rust. It does not link against, wrap, or embed OpenSSL.

Archaeological material
-----------------------

Upstream OpenSSL source releases are used strictly as *archaeological
authority material*: to enumerate the public contract (headers, symbol
inventories, provider and CLI surface) against which the candidate is
compared. The admitted authorities are recorded, with verified SHA-256
checksums and content-addressed source manifests, in:

    forensics/authorities/AUTHORITIES.json

The upstream project and its licence:

    OpenSSL
    https://www.openssl.org/
    Apache License 2.0 (OpenSSL 3.x)

OpenSSL source is not redistributed as part of the candidate implementation,
and implementation is reasoned from behavioural obligations rather than
mechanically transliterated from C. See docs/CUSTODIAN_CONTRACT.md §3
("Provenance rule").

Generated compatibility surface
-------------------------------

Public headers, symbol version scripts and related declarations for the
candidate will be *generated* from the authority atlas. Where any interface
material derived from OpenSSL is emitted, the applicable OpenSSL licence and
attribution will be carried with it.

Third-party components
----------------------

The candidate crate has no dependencies (see Cargo.toml). This is a contract,
not an accident: the dependency surface is enforced by
forensics/tools/check_forbidden_dependencies.py.

Court tooling
-------------

Evidence tooling (Python, shell, C probes) exercises independent
implementations only as *test authorities* and interoperability peers inside
the court container. No such implementation is ever a hidden product backend.

This project's own licence: Apache-2.0 OR MIT.
